{"type":"text","timestamp":1794540672602,"sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b66ffeBll9TqHwuHOQnJ","part":{"id":"prt_1d2f582b1002rGGkNMzmWI8W26","sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b66ffeBll9TqHwuHOQnJ","messageID":"msg_1d2f577ea001vvlpzchc1JviZU","type":"text","text":"## T015 complete\n\n**File written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` (`CAP`)\n\nWhat changed there:\n- The dynamic import of the built attach module now also pulls `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS`.\n- Each `row_type: 'typed'` row computes `delivered = typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached` and `policy = TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`, then feeds a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` / `addAttachedRow` (`own` on `top1Hit`, else `attached` when the delivered command matches `expected_command` and the policy is non-null).\n- `attachedMetrics.typed` (via `attachedTallyJson`) and `attachedMetrics.typedRows` were added. `typedRows` is keyed by row id in sorted order with exactly `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }` and carries no prompt text. Every pre-existing key and computation is untouched.\n\n**Build** (required by the task's \"after `BLD`\"): `npm run build` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` exited successfully; the rebuild refreshed the gitignored `dist/`, which is why `typedCommandForTop` is now present in `dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'\n{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}\n\n$ node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'\n[[\"carried\",\"command\",\"expected_command\",\"policy\",\"top\"]]\n\n$ node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'\n{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}\n{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}\n```\n\nSupplementary check: `typedRows` holds 44 rows with `carried` split `{\"attached\":20,\"own\":24}`.\n\n**Not done**\n- The `T015` checkbox in `tasks.md` is deliberately left unticked.\n- Nothing else in my scope was blocked. The other modified files visible under `runtime/` belong to other workers; I did not touch them, and the `dist/` output is generated by the build the task requires.","time":{"start":1794540667569,"end":1794540672602}}}
